// CROWN — two independent callers of one generic HOF: one declares `!E`
// and passes a pure closure, the other declares nothing and performs E.
// Must accept.
//
// Accepted through the pinned boot (runs 10). The guard on bounds crossing
// an instantiation: `g`'s negation must bind its own copy of `apply`'s
// parameter, never `apply`'s declaration, or `h` would be refused.
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn apply(f) = f()
fn g() with !E = apply(() => 3)
fn h() = apply(() => op())
handler hh { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = (g() + h()) ~> hh
